        paragraphs: ["A PM2.5 Analyzer is used to continuously measure fine particulate matter with aerodynamic diameter ≤2.5 microns (PM2.5) present in ambient air. These ultra-fine particles can penetrate deep into the lungs and bloodstream, making PM2.5 a critical air quality parameter for environmental and public health monitoring.","The analyzer is installed with a PM2.5 size-selective inlet, sampling system, and control unit for reliable long-term outdoor operation."],
        bullets: ["Working Principle: PM2.5 analyzers typically operate using: Beta Attenuation Method (BAM): Measures particle mass by beta radiation absorption through collected particles. Optical / Light Scattering Method: Determines particle concentration by analyzing scattered light. Only particles ≤2.5 µm are allowed through the inlet for measurement."]
